            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-26T00:33:46.36083+00:00",
            "notes": "The core gimmick of this build is to combine [Frost Armor](item_f9925f6e-bb6a-4de6-bb86-622583d60779) with [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) for an efficiently-priced pool of self-regenerating Armor. However, since that gimmick is out of reach until *at least* Round 2, it's better to start off with pure damage so you can farm more $ and hopefully secure a few eliminations.\n\nTo that end, [Extendothermics](item_501fc89f-a7b4-46c5-a43f-b65ab0958438) will give you an early edge. You're still gonna want to launch icicles until a brawl breaks out, but once you've properly engaged the enemy, having a +60% range boost to your ultra-reliable primary fire is huge. Whether you're chasing or kiting, this power helps you to maintain optimal positioning.\n\nAs for starting items, [Ammo Reserves](item_982d53aa-5ef4-493f-93e7-9e374d0ebf34), [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf), and [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) are the way to go. If you're winning, win harder. If you're losing, ice block. Don't bother building for Armor or Lifesteal until Round 3.",
